From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:59:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Soloud::mixBus_internal: a ticking voice clears the rest of a
 short block

The mixing path clears the part of a resample block that the source did
not fill; the inaudible ticking path did not, so the block kept the audio
read into it two blocks before. A voice made audible again while it was
on such a block (its last one, for a sound that ends) played that audio
after the end of the sound, up to the rest of the block. The ticking path
now clears it too.
---
 src/core/soloud.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud.cpp b/src/core/soloud.cpp
index 5ff90c6..5cd5da0 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud.cpp
@@ -1939,6 +1939,15 @@ namespace SoLoud
 						}
 						voice->mBlockSamples = readcount;
 
+						// Nothing reads the block while the voice ticks, but it plays
+						// the rest of it if it becomes audible: clear what was not read.
+						if (readcount < SAMPLE_GRANULARITY)
+						{
+							unsigned int k;
+							for (k = 0; k < voice->mChannels; k++)
+								memset(voice->mResampleData[0] + readcount + SAMPLE_GRANULARITY * k, 0, sizeof(float) * (SAMPLE_GRANULARITY - readcount));
+						}
+
 						// If we go past zero, crop to zero (a bit of a kludge)
 						if (voice->mSrcOffset < SAMPLE_GRANULARITY * FIXPOINT_FRAC_MUL)
 						{
